# Version bumping (REQUIRED)

`src/version.ts` → `APP_VERSION` is the **single source of truth**. Nothing else
may define a version string; `package.json` and the Settings dialog derive from it.

Before finishing any task that changes code, config, or docs, run exactly one
bump:

```bash
npm run version:bump -- <patch|minor|major> "short summary of the change set"
```

That updates `APP_VERSION`, prepends a `VERSION_HISTORY` entry, and syncs
`package.json`. Never hand-edit the version numbers.

## Level — judge the whole change set, take the highest

- **MAJOR** — breaks stored data, a storage/API contract, or needs a migration
  (e.g. changing the IndexedDB or server storage format, changing the `/ics`
  proxy contract, removing a feature).
- **MINOR** — something new or user-visible changed (e.g. a new component, hook,
  module or exported function; a new dependency; a different default date range;
  changed ICS parsing or sync behaviour).
- **PATCH** — fixes and maintenance only (bug fix with no contract change,
  comments, docs, formatting, tests, behaviour-preserving refactor).

Exactly **one** bump per task; never skip a level. Many changes are still one
bump — but if any of them is breaking, the task is MAJOR. When torn between two
levels, pick the higher one.

## Verify

`npm run version:check` must pass; `npm test` includes
`src/__tests__/version.test.ts`; `npm run build` runs `version:check` first.

Full policy: `VERSION.md`. General repo rules: `AGENTS.md`.
